    "grade": "9-10",
    "points": 3,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "What is the value of $x$ such that $(x + 2^{2018})^2 - (x - 2^{2018})^2 = 2^{2019}$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$1$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$2^2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$2^{2020}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$2^{-1}$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Difference of squares",
        "body": "$(x+a)^2 - (x-a)^2 = \\big((x+a)+(x-a)\\big)\\big((x+a)-(x-a)\\big) = 2x\\cdot 2a = 4ax$. With $a = 2^{2018}$: $4\\cdot 2^{2018}\\,x = 2^{2020}x = 2^{2019}$, so $x = 2^{-1}$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $2^{-1}$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Expand",
        "body": "$(x+a)^2 = x^2 + 2ax + a^2$ and $(x-a)^2 = x^2 - 2ax + a^2$; the difference is $4ax = 2^{2020}x$. Setting it equal to $2^{2019}$ gives $x = \\frac12 = 2^{-1}$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $2^{-1}$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "algebra"
    ],
    "difficulty": 1,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
