    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "On a certain day 40 trains each travelled between two of the towns $M$, $N$, $O$, $P$ and $Q$. 12 trains travelled either from or to $M$. 12 trains travelled either from or to $N$. 12 trains travelled either from or to $O$. 12 trains travelled either from or to $P$. How many trains travelled from or to $Q$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "24"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "32"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "36"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "40"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count train ends",
        "body": "Every train has two end towns, so the five \"from or to\" counts add up to $2\\cdot 40 = 80$. M, N, O and P account for $4\\cdot 12 = 48$, so Q accounts for $80 - 48 = 32$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 32**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Trains not touching Q",
        "body": "Let $t$ be the number of trains not touching Q. Each such train is counted twice among the 48 counts of M, N, O, P, while each train touching Q is counted once. So $2t + (40 - t) = 48$, giving $t = 8$ and $40 - 8 = 32$ trains touching Q.\n\n**Answer: (C) 32**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "logic",
      "graph-theory"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
