    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Let $M$ be the sum of all odd positive integers less than 100, and let $K$ be the sum of all even positive numbers less than or equal to 100. What is $K - M$?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "50"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "100"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "0"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "−100"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "−50"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pair the terms",
        "body": "$K - M = (2 - 1) + (4 - 3) + \\dots + (100 - 99)$, which is 50 differences of 1. So $K - M = 50$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 50**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Compute both sums",
        "body": "$M = 1 + 3 + \\dots + 99 = 50^2 = 2500$ and $K = 2 + 4 + \\dots + 100 = 2(1 + \\dots + 50) = 2550$. So $K - M = 50$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 50**"
      }
    ],
